WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.169
The SCP Foundation has a reputation for cold,
inhumane conditions, but being contained as

00:00:06.169 --> 00:00:10.690
an anomalous human doesn’t mean your stay
inside a secure facility has to be as bad

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:12.410
as it might seem at first.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:18.350
Of course, more dangerous anomalous entities,
such as SCP-076, codenamed Able, are locked

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:23.110
away in a containment chamber outfitted with
maximum security precautions and guarded by

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:28.530
the Foundation’s most well-trained and heavily
armed personnel, but not every anomaly poses

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.380
a danger, and the Foundation realizes that.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:38.540
Sure, the monsters like SCP-106 or SCP-096,
who need no introduction, aren’t exactly

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:42.899
treated to a bed and breakfast every morning,
but those lower on the danger scale can get

00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:47.510
pretty comfortable inside their new home,
depending on how well they’ve behaved and

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:50.120
how little of a threat they pose, of course.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:57.530
Take for instance SCP-076’s less violent
brother, SCP-073, also known as Cain.

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:04.100
SCP-073 is peaceful, a complete contrast to
SCP-076’s destructive fits of violence and

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:09.600
rage, and as a result, he’s treated like
nearly any other low-threat anomalous humanoid.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.020
Amenities, clothes, maybe even some time in
the Foundation’s recreational spaces if

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:17.850
they’re extra well-behaved, it’s true
that the Foundation has been doing a lot for

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:22.060
the anomalies it contains, especially in recent
years.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:27.100
After all, anomalies contained by the Foundation
are, containment breaches aside, supposed

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.020
to be contained for life.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:33.600
The least the Foundation can do with all of
their seemingly infinite money and funding

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.760
is show them an easier time while they’re
there.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:41.329
Sometimes, anomalous humanoids are integrated
into the Foundation’s command structure.

00:01:41.329 --> 00:01:46.630
Such is the case with the mysterious Dr. Clef,
a former Global Occult Coalition agent turned

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:51.810
Foundation operative with reality bending
powers and a penchant for neutralizing dangerous

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:52.810
anomalies.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:58.039
Or Dr. Jack Bright, who continued to work
as a Foundation researcher following an accident

00:01:58.039 --> 00:02:03.430
with SCP-963, an amulet that made his consciousness
immortal.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:08.890
Or Kain Pathos Crow, once an ordinary Foundation
scientist, now a golden retriever blessed

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:14.690
with super-intelligence thanks to an experiment
gone wrong, or right, depending on who you

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:15.690
ask.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:19.440
It’s true, the Foundation is definitely
more accepting of the anomalous than it may

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:20.790
initially seem.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:25.830
Let’s take a look at a particularly notable
anomaly contained by the Foundation, SCP-166.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:31.030
SCP-166 can be seen as a baseline example
of how the Foundation treats the average humanoid

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:36.300
anomaly that doesn’t pose a significant
threat to the organization or society at large.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:42.690
SCP-166 is contained at the famous Site-19
inside a hermetically sealed antechamber outfitted

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:45.200
with an industrial air purifier.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:50.620
Personnel assigned to SCP-166’s containment
chamber must wear specially designated biohazard

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:57.430
suits before entering, and keep them on at
all times, lest they succumb to SCP-166’s

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:58.430
anomalous effects.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:05.410
SCP-166 is a teenage girl of european descent,
possessing certain bodily features found on

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:06.450
a reindeer.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.820
She has antlers, hooved feet, and a short
tail.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:11.920
All that’s missing is a red nose, right?

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.600
But despite looking like one of Santa’s
most trusted four-legged helpers, SCP-166

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:19.060
has little to do with the animal.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:22.860
In fact, scans of her DNA reveal no irregular
genetic traits.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:27.750
To the instruments used to record such things,
she's a completely ordinary human.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:32.110
Her reindeer features are, according to some
Foundation theorists, a reflection of her

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:35.120
connection with nature, and a remnant of her
past.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.830
But we’ll get to that.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:42.290
Aside from her fluffy parts, what makes SCP-166
so anomalous?

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:48.420
As it turns out, SCP-166 possesses an incredibly
strong anomalous ability.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:53.120
Any artificial objects, meaning those that
are man-made, within a 15 meter radius of

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.060
SCP-166 will return to an unworked state.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:02.530
For example, a car placed within SCP-166’s
range will return to a composite of paint,

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:05.700
metals, leather, and plastics over time.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:10.680
These higher complexity objects, such as vehicles
or electronics, are affected more quickly

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:16.850
by SCP-166, with degradation of their metallic
components giving out and causing massive

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:21.049
structural failure, resulting in an unusable
object.

00:04:21.049 --> 00:04:25.680
More natural objects made of rudimentary materials,
such as stone buildings and products made

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.520
of organic materials will decay at a much
slower, nearly imperceptible rate.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:36.380
So SCP-166’s containment chamber and containment
situation is more than safe, though it might

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:39.710
need to be repaired and touched up over the
years.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:45.280
SCP-166 is very in touch with nature, as her
appearance would suggest.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:50.130
In fact, in areas where objects degraded as
a result of her influence, flowers and plant

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:52.220
growth will begin to appear.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:57.160
Sometimes this foliage will grow in places
that should otherwise be impossible for it

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:00.350
to, such as ID scanners or security cameras.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:04.170
You could imagine that the inside of the chamber
is practically a botanical garden.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:10.850
Still, the Foundation has to be careful with
how SCP-166’s containment chamber is constructed,

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:16.220
and who enters it, as the degrading deer-girl
harbors a particular sensitivity to artificial

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:20.780
materials and pollutants, such as smoke or
pesticides.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:27.590
Inhalation of, or contact with one of these
airy substances causes SCP-166 to grow ulcers,

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:30.180
and suffer symptoms of asthma attacks.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:36.360
Even being in close proximity with a smoker
can cause SCP-166 pain, with one instance

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:41.200
prompting a severe asthma attack despite the
Foundation doctor in question having not smoked

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.880
a cigarette in over three weeks.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:47.620
If you need another reason to stay away from
smoking, do it for SCP-166.

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:50.230
Isn’t she adorable?

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:53.120
You wouldn’t want to give her a panic attack,
would you?

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:58.490
Not only are SCP-166’s visitors limited
and screened beforehand, but her clothing

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:02.830
consists of organic cloth, so as not to trigger
a degradation effect.

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:07.300
All of her meals must be prepared by a trained
Foundation chef and followed according to

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:12.230
a specific set of guidelines, with as little
inorganic additives as possible.

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:16.430
The Foundation has to be a little bit more
careful than usual with the items requested

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:22.780
by SCP-166, not only due to her anomalous
ability to degrade objects, but due to her

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:26.800
mysterious past and connection with a small
convent of nuns in Ireland.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:27.800
We’ll explain.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:34.130
You see, like most humanoid anomalies, the
Foundation has allowed SCP-166 to put in requests

00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:37.340
for personal items she might find missing
from her containment.

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:41.530
Now, the Foundation may deny these items,
for a variety of reasons, but there’s also

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:42.990
a chance they won’t.

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:49.040
To date, SCP-166 has requested a copy of the
Holy Bible, a Catholic rosary, and various

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:53.560
books and magazines involving religious content,
all of which were approved by Site-19’s

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:56.240
director Sophia Light.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:07:02.790
SCP-166 also requested access to a Catholic
priest for confession, mass, and other sacraments.

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:07.860
This request was initially denied, but later
reapproved after Chaplain Davis, an ordained

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:13.940
member of the clergy working with the Foundation,
agreed to meet with SCP-166 on a bi-weekly

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:16.730
schedule, every other Sunday.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:22.210
SCP-166 also requested a telephone, which
she intended to use to contact the Abbess

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:28.240
of the Our Lady of Mercy Convent, a cloistered
society of nuns in County Galway, Ireland.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:31.389
This request was a little more complicated
to process.

00:07:31.389 --> 00:07:36.090
At first it was denied, then granted, and
then denied again after a reconsideration

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:37.370
by Director Light.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:41.140
But why did SCP-166 want this item?

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:45.330
What connection could the deer girl have to
a group of nuns in Ireland?

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:47.270
The answers lie in the Foundation’s discovery
of SCP-166.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:56.050
SCP-166 was discovered in the Our Lady of
Mercy Convent, in County Galway, Ireland,

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:58.970
where the girl had been living since infancy.

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:03.460
Her strange appearance and abilities initially
made her the subject of scrutiny by the sisters

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:08.440
who lived there, but she was taken care of,
and raised as a member of the Catholic faith.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:14.389
When the Foundation was alerted to SCP-166’s
existence, a defecting Global Occult Coalition

00:08:14.389 --> 00:08:19.040
agent operating under the codename “Ukulele”,
who was now in the process of joining the

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:23.729
Foundation, confirmed that he recognized SCP-166.

00:08:23.729 --> 00:08:29.650
He knew that SCP-166 was the child of an incredibly
dangerous entity, classified by the Global

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:35.940
Occult Coalition as Threat Entity 9927-Black,
a being codenamed "The Goddess".

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:40.339
The Goddess also was being pursued by the
SCP Foundation, and given a designation as

00:08:40.339 --> 00:08:45.709
an SCP object, though its number and the exact
details of the file have been redacted by

00:08:45.709 --> 00:08:48.320
the Foundation for security purposes.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:53.260
What we do know is that The Goddess was a
seriously dangerous entity, and both parties

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:59.180
were dedicating as many resources as possible
to its capture, containment, or neutralization.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:03.980
The conflict between The Goddess, the Global
Occult Coalition, and the SCP Foundation came

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:07.709
to a head during an event known as the Cornwall
Incident.

00:09:07.709 --> 00:09:12.389
The Goddess’s file, which was received and
archived by the SCP Foundation has a portion

00:09:12.389 --> 00:09:16.430
describing SCP-166, which reads as follows:

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:23.670
“Threat entity is the child of incarnated
LTE-9927-Black ("The Goddess") and an unknown

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:24.670
father.

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:28.129
While it strongly resembles its mother and
shares its animalistic features, it lacks

00:09:28.129 --> 00:09:31.880
the extreme bestial appearance of 9927-Black.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:36.470
Possesses minor chlorokinetic abilities, but
primary reason for threat entity classification

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:41.430
is the instinctive knowledge and eligibility
to enact Occult Procedure Clockwork Blackchild

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:45.980
Havilah, a world-wide ritual working that
would irreversibly regress human civilization

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:47.560
to Neolithic standards.”

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:52.379
“Strike Team "Lancelot" neutralized 9927-Black
in England during an operation which would

00:09:52.379 --> 00:09:57.329
later be known as the infamous 'Cornwall Incident',
but were unable to confirm the liquidation

00:09:57.329 --> 00:10:02.249
of 9927-Blackchild due to the death of the
strike leader, Agent Ukulele.

00:10:02.249 --> 00:10:08.079
Ukulele was posthumously awarded the Silver
Aegis for his lifelong service to humanity.”

00:10:08.079 --> 00:10:14.029
As the file stated, SCP-166 is the child of
The Goddess, and the reason for her anomalous

00:10:14.029 --> 00:10:19.149
degradation abilities is so that she can enact
them on the world and fulfill her mother’s

00:10:19.149 --> 00:10:20.410
unholy mission.

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:26.009
A ritual that would regress society to prehistoric
times, ridding the world of modern technology

00:10:26.009 --> 00:10:28.020
and manmade creations.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:34.339
Why The Goddess wanted to carry out this ritual
is unknown, but SCP-166 was her key to achieving

00:10:34.339 --> 00:10:36.439
her primitive desires.

00:10:36.439 --> 00:10:40.920
Through her child, she could reach her goals,
but the Cornwall Incident threw a wrench in

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:42.749
the Goddess’s plans.

00:10:42.749 --> 00:10:47.279
Agent Ukulele, a Global Occult Agent famous
for decommissioning dangerous anomalies, was

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:50.350
tasked with killing SCP-166.

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:55.310
Perhaps it was her human appearance, or the
fact that she was only a small child, or even

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:57.690
something that lied even deeper.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:11:01.269
Ukulele could not bring himself to terminate
SCP-166.

00:11:01.269 --> 00:11:07.800
He defected from the Global Occult Coalition,
faking his death and taking SCP-166 alongside

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:08.800
him.

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:14.050
Entrusting her care to the convent of nuns,
Ukulele made himself scarce, relieved that

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:16.860
SCP-166 was safe.

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:21.399
After being free from the Global Occult Coalition’s
grasp, Ukulele was unsure of what to do with

00:11:21.399 --> 00:11:22.519
his life.

00:11:22.519 --> 00:11:27.639
Taking the name “Alto Clef”, Ukulele had
rid his previous identity from the anomalous

00:11:27.639 --> 00:11:30.399
world, and was prepared to start a new life.

00:11:30.399 --> 00:11:34.079
But he couldn’t let SCP-166 live unattended.

00:11:34.079 --> 00:11:38.199
What if the Global Occult Coalition found
her, and terminated her in an act that would

00:11:38.199 --> 00:11:41.220
finish what they had started all those years
ago?

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:42.809
What if the Foundation discovered her?

00:11:42.809 --> 00:11:46.779
He didn’t want to risk the girl being put
into a life of containment that she never

00:11:46.779 --> 00:11:47.779
wanted.

00:11:47.779 --> 00:11:53.389
Clef decided he made the best decision, and
kept SCP-166’s existence to himself as best

00:11:53.389 --> 00:11:54.389
he could.

00:11:54.389 --> 00:11:57.140
But his hand was forced not long after.

00:11:57.140 --> 00:12:03.079
SCP-166, at the age of 12, was seen by a civilian
visiting the convent, who reported her existence

00:12:03.079 --> 00:12:04.480
to the authorities.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:07.110
The Foundation became aware of SCP-166.

00:12:07.110 --> 00:12:13.709
Clef, wanting the best for SCP-166, exchanged
valuable Global Occult Coalition intelligence,

00:12:13.709 --> 00:12:19.610
documents, and information with The Foundation
in exchange for SCP-166’s containment and

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:20.809
guaranteed safety.

00:12:20.809 --> 00:12:23.420
It was the best he could do for the girl.

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:28.730
Clef then fully defected to the SCP Foundation,
where his skills were heavily in demand.

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:33.750
Soon, SCP-166 was retrieved from the convent
and brought into containment.

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:36.709
At least now, Clef could know she was safe.

00:12:36.709 --> 00:12:40.929
The Cornwall Incident resulted in the termination
of the Goddess, and all parties were relieved

00:12:40.929 --> 00:12:45.589
that the world was rid of this dangerous and
mysterious entity, but it also brought Clef

00:12:45.589 --> 00:12:47.749
a significant amount of strife.

00:12:47.749 --> 00:12:50.819
Why did he save SCP-166?

00:12:50.819 --> 00:12:54.759
Why was the battle-hardened and brutal assassin
unable to kill her?

00:12:54.759 --> 00:12:58.699
What connection did Clef share with the Goddess,
if any?

00:12:58.699 --> 00:13:02.410
SCP-166 often wondered about the exact details
of her past.

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:06.520
She wasn’t privy to her history with Clef,
or all of the details of her birth, or what

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:09.709
arcane ritual she was born to carry out.

00:13:09.709 --> 00:13:14.869
SCP-166 only knew the convent, her faith in
the Catholic religion, and her life in the

00:13:14.869 --> 00:13:17.750
custody of the SCP Foundation.

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:21.429
During her talks with Chaplain Davis, she
often discussed these feelings and desires

00:13:21.429 --> 00:13:24.069
to know more about herself and her past.

00:13:24.069 --> 00:13:28.629
The Foundation kept further details about
the Goddess and her past under restrictive

00:13:28.629 --> 00:13:34.459
classifications, and attempts to pry deeper
never bore SCP-166 any fruit.

00:13:34.459 --> 00:13:40.399
One conversation between SCP-166 and Chaplain
Davis was particularly noteworthy.

00:13:40.399 --> 00:13:44.670
Inside the small confessional, where the two
met every other week, they exchanged greetings

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:46.369
and began talking.

00:13:46.369 --> 00:13:51.739
SCP-166 enjoyed her talks with Chaplain Davis,
which allowed her to explore her faith and

00:13:51.739 --> 00:13:53.899
further her appreciation of it.

00:13:53.899 --> 00:13:58.100
It also gave her an opportunity to talk about
her feelings and thoughts in an environment

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:00.459
similar to the one she was raised in.

00:14:00.459 --> 00:14:06.049
To start, Davis reminded SCP-166 that information
she gave him could be reported higher up in

00:14:06.049 --> 00:14:08.149
the Foundation, if need be.

00:14:08.149 --> 00:14:12.949
In the Catholic religion, confession is a
confidential space, but for the SCP Foundation,

00:14:12.949 --> 00:14:16.050
the rules of the church are often broken.

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:20.970
“As usual, I have to remind you that due
to our environment, the seal of confession

00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:24.439
will not take place unless specifically invoked.

00:14:24.439 --> 00:14:28.939
Even then, details of our conversation can
be unsealed if they're determined to be essential.

00:14:28.939 --> 00:14:29.939
Understand?”

00:14:29.939 --> 00:14:30.980
Davis said.

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:34.209
SCP-166 understood, and nodded her head.

00:14:34.209 --> 00:14:39.809
First, SCP-166 asked a question about a replacement
for Pope Benedict, who had announced his retirement

00:14:39.809 --> 00:14:41.209
at the time of the interview.

00:14:41.209 --> 00:14:45.640
Chaplain Davis responded:
“Ah, yes, that was rather unfortunate, but

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:47.010
it does make sense.

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:50.509
He was rather old even when he first took
up the position.

00:14:50.509 --> 00:14:54.300
Now he can rest, knowing he served the Church
well.”

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:58.160
SCP-166 was curious to know if a replacement
had been decided.

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:02.850
Davis informed her that while there was speculation,
one had yet to be decided for certain.

00:15:02.850 --> 00:15:06.949
Though he was sure the Church would want to
go forward with a fresh, new face to broaden

00:15:06.949 --> 00:15:08.220
its mission.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:13.639
SCP-166 seemed pleased at this, but Chaplain
Davis sensed an underlying discomfort in the

00:15:13.639 --> 00:15:14.639
girl.

00:15:14.639 --> 00:15:16.649
She wasn’t speaking her true feelings.

00:15:16.649 --> 00:15:20.899
He assured her that whatever questions she
had, he could answer to the best of his abilities

00:15:20.899 --> 00:15:22.810
and without any judgement.

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:25.980
SCP-166 decided to speak up.

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:29.980
She wanted to know if Chaplain Davis had a
good relationship with his parents.

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:34.819
Davis sat back for a moment and thought carefully
about his response, as he did with all questions

00:15:34.819 --> 00:15:38.959
that could cause an emotional response in
SCP-166.

00:15:38.959 --> 00:15:44.690
No topic was more sensitive for SCP-166 than
the matter of her heritage.

00:15:44.690 --> 00:15:48.699
Davis informed her that he maintained a good
relationship with his mother before she passed

00:15:48.699 --> 00:15:51.980
away, and a less than happy relationship with
his father.

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:57.629
Davis asked about SCP-166’s parents, diverting
the conversation away from himself.

00:15:57.629 --> 00:16:03.109
He wasn’t sure, at this point, exactly how
much SCP-166 was told or knew.

00:16:03.109 --> 00:16:08.459
In fact, the Foundation didn’t even let
Chaplain Davis know the full context of SCP-166’s

00:16:08.459 --> 00:16:09.459
origins.

00:16:09.459 --> 00:16:13.410
“I never really knew my parents,” said
SCP-166.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:15.470
“I got dropped off when I was a baby.

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:19.959
I mean, I guess they must've known the sisters
if they put me there, but I don't remember

00:16:19.959 --> 00:16:20.959
them.

00:16:20.959 --> 00:16:21.959
Just what I picked up.

00:16:21.959 --> 00:16:24.630
They mentioned my mother a bit, before they
realized that they should watch what they

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:25.630
say about me.

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:28.459
I think they said something about her being
a goddess?

00:16:28.459 --> 00:16:32.269
Which obviously wouldn't be true, she must've
been some sort of spirit, but she must've

00:16:32.269 --> 00:16:34.929
been something if I ended up looking like
this.

00:16:34.929 --> 00:16:38.880
I remember eavesdropping on the Abbess, she
was talking to one of the other sisters about

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:43.290
how she had done something wrong, something
about a ritual that someone else stopped.

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:44.600
They said she died.”

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:50.869
Davis, taken back by SCP-166’s revelations,
told the girl that he was sorry for her loss.

00:16:50.869 --> 00:16:55.600
SCP-166 said that it wasn’t like she knew
her anyway, so she wasn’t bothered by it

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:56.670
that much.

00:16:56.670 --> 00:17:02.089
Davis asked about her father, but SCP-166
also had little information on him.

00:17:02.089 --> 00:17:06.309
She said that she had asked the Abbess about
him multiple times, but she never mentioned

00:17:06.309 --> 00:17:08.649
SCP-166’s father.

00:17:08.649 --> 00:17:13.179
She wondered, if her mother, the Goddess,
was so horrible, what did her father do that

00:17:13.179 --> 00:17:15.579
made him unspeakable?

00:17:15.579 --> 00:17:19.299
SCP-166’s questions would not go unanswered.

00:17:19.299 --> 00:17:22.220
One day, a letter was found inside her containment
area.

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:25.029
It read:
“I first met your mother when we were little

00:17:25.029 --> 00:17:26.029
more than children.

00:17:26.029 --> 00:17:29.450
She had hooves for feet and starlight in her
eyes.

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:34.149
She was beauty and nature incarnate, and I
killed her with my own two hands.

00:17:34.149 --> 00:17:36.100
Eden isn't a place.

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:37.610
It's a state of being.

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:40.799
They wanted to take us back to it, and I stopped
them.

00:17:40.799 --> 00:17:43.710
I took paradise away from us for a second
time.

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:49.040
I have never regretted my actions on that
day, except one: that when you first met me

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:53.640
on that day, you saw your father put a bullet
into the head of your mother.

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:56.240
I make no excuses, only explanation.

00:17:56.240 --> 00:18:02.110
You may not have even remembered it, but I'm
telling you now in the hope you understand

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:03.769
why I did what I did.

00:18:03.769 --> 00:18:05.330
I hope you forgive me.

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:06.330
I love you.

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:08.279
I wish I could have done more for you.

00:18:08.279 --> 00:18:12.850
The best I could do was leave you in the hands
of kind and loving people and hope they would

00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:14.130
raise you in my place.

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:16.130
From what I've seen, they did well.

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:18.049
I'm sorry you couldn't stay with them.

00:18:18.049 --> 00:18:20.279
I'm sorry they've brought you to this place.

00:18:20.279 --> 00:18:24.960
I promise to do my best to make sure your
stay here is pleasant.

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:26.850
I promise to keep you safe.”

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:29.980
“Happy sixteenth birthday, from your loving
father.

00:18:29.980 --> 00:18:33.429
Dr. Clef”
Site-19’s Director, Sophia Light, gave Clef

00:18:33.429 --> 00:18:39.520
a disciplinary interview for making unapproved
contact with SCP-166 and writing such an emotional

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:40.990
appeal to the girl.

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:46.539
Clef had been barred from talking to SCP-166,
and his superiors were even skeptical about

00:18:46.539 --> 00:18:48.990
letting him work at the same site as her.

00:18:48.990 --> 00:18:51.330
Light showed sympathy for Clef’s dilemma.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:57.660
For 16 years, SCP-166, Clef’s daughter,
was unable to live her life normally because

00:18:57.660 --> 00:18:59.400
of who she was.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:01.409
He felt partially responsible.

00:19:01.409 --> 00:19:05.650
Despite being one of the Foundation’s most
trusted and powerful agents, capable of sending

00:19:05.650 --> 00:19:10.260
a strike team anywhere in the world and knowing
secrets people would pay billions to know,

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:12.940
Clef was unable to talk to his own daughter.

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:17.750
In the end, Clef was subject to a minor disciplinary
infraction, but the hope that he may one day

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:20.850
reunite with his beloved SCP-166 remains.

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:28.149
Now go check out “SCP-407 - The Song of
Genesis” and “SCP-6000 - The Serpent,

00:19:28.149 --> 00:19:32.730
the Moose and the Wanderer's Library” for
more nature-inspired SCPs.

